1
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Changhuan.

2
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:20,500
We're here.

3
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:23,500
"The Last Oath"

4
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,500
(Episode 13: Post-Outbreak
Infection Research)

5
00:02:34,666 --> 00:02:35,666
Sleep well last night?

6
00:02:38,041 --> 00:02:39,041
Yeah.

7
00:02:57,250 --> 00:02:58,250
Not again.

8
00:02:58,666 --> 00:02:59,666
It's torn open.

9
00:03:04,083 --> 00:03:05,457
I'm talking about your wound.

10
00:03:05,458 --> 00:03:06,458
What were you thinking?

11
00:03:09,166 --> 00:03:10,166
I'm fine.

12
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:11,250
It doesn't hurt anymore.

13
00:03:11,416 --> 00:03:12,416
My fever's gone too.

14
00:03:23,125 --> 00:03:24,205
Let's get down to business.

15
00:03:25,916 --> 00:03:27,083
He Yao drove the car away.

16
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:29,166
What do we do now?

17
00:03:30,375 --> 00:03:31,541
If we follow the highway,

18
00:03:31,916 --> 00:03:33,516
we should be able to find a working car.

19
00:04:10,166 --> 00:04:11,166
Let's go.

20
00:04:35,541 --> 00:04:36,541
Walk properly.

21
00:04:47,583 --> 00:04:49,383
What's wrong? Did your
wound tear open again?

22
00:04:54,166 --> 00:04:55,166
How childish can you be?

23
00:04:56,223 --> 00:04:56,848
Very childish.

24
00:04:57,261 --> 00:04:58,261
So what?

25
00:05:00,541 --> 00:05:01,541
Big baby.

26
00:05:36,083 --> 00:05:37,083
This place...

27
00:05:37,208 --> 00:05:38,666
is actually pretty well-preserved.

28
00:05:39,284 --> 00:05:40,284
Yeah.

29
00:05:40,375 --> 00:05:41,375
Let's take a break.

30
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,375
For a split second just now,

31
00:06:08,208 --> 00:06:10,008
I thought we were back
before the apocalypse.

32
00:06:12,166 --> 00:06:13,166
It felt like...

33
00:06:14,083 --> 00:06:15,458
this was just a normal date.

34
00:06:18,041 --> 00:06:19,601
Did you come to places like this often?

35
00:06:22,041 --> 00:06:23,041
Do you mean...

36
00:06:23,125 --> 00:06:24,125
on dates,

37
00:06:24,375 --> 00:06:25,375
or to watch performances?

38
00:06:34,250 --> 00:06:35,291
This is my first date.

39
00:06:35,916 --> 00:06:37,916
I rarely went to performances before, either.

40
00:06:41,541 --> 00:06:43,341
Have you ever experienced
anything like this?

41
00:06:49,541 --> 00:06:50,541
Let's eat first.

42
00:07:03,666 --> 00:07:04,666
You're so lazy.

43
00:07:15,125 --> 00:07:16,125
This...

44
00:07:49,125 --> 00:07:50,125
It's fine.

45
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:51,500
It's far enough away.

46
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:31,999
I didn't expect zombies to retain

47
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,640
the skills they had when they were alive.

48
00:08:41,541 --> 00:08:42,541
Tell me,

49
00:08:42,791 --> 00:08:45,364
do you think zombies might still have
a little bit of human consciousness left?

50
00:08:47,250 --> 00:08:48,375
Is it possible that one day,

51
00:08:50,583 --> 00:08:52,023
zombies could turn back into humans?

52
00:08:55,708 --> 00:08:56,708
It's just muscle memory.

53
00:08:58,458 --> 00:08:59,875
Zombies are zombies.

54
00:09:01,416 --> 00:09:02,416
They can't turn back.

55
00:11:29,458 --> 00:11:30,458
Where are we?

56
00:11:35,041 --> 00:11:36,041
He Yao,

57
00:11:37,791 --> 00:11:39,151
what exactly are you trying to do?

58
00:11:43,333 --> 00:11:45,250
Stop feeding me this useless stuff.

59
00:11:48,958 --> 00:11:49,958
There's no going back.

60
00:11:52,208 --> 00:11:53,208
I know that myself.

61
00:11:56,125 --> 00:11:57,125
I have a plan.

62
00:11:57,666 --> 00:11:58,666
Just give me some time.

63
00:11:59,208 --> 00:12:00,458
The equipment here is old,

64
00:12:00,602 --> 00:12:01,559
but it works perfectly...

65
00:12:01,584 --> 00:12:02,875
He Yao, you're always like this.

66
00:12:05,125 --> 00:12:07,416
Always acting like you have
everything under control.

67
00:12:08,875 --> 00:12:10,332
But when have you ever cared

68
00:12:10,333 --> 00:12:11,333
about what others think?

69
00:12:14,416 --> 00:12:15,583
Do you know

70
00:12:17,833 --> 00:12:19,458
that the way you are right now

71
00:12:21,375 --> 00:12:24,125
is exactly like when you
suddenly barged into my life?

72
00:12:26,541 --> 00:12:27,541
Leave.

73
00:12:27,875 --> 00:12:29,000
Get out of here.

74
00:12:29,333 --> 00:12:30,666
I don't want to see you.

75
00:12:49,750 --> 00:12:50,750
Yao,

76
00:12:51,166 --> 00:12:53,416
this will be your home from now on.

77
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Make yourself at home.

78
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:00,083
Changhuan is back.

79
00:13:01,291 --> 00:13:02,291
Come here.

80
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,374
This is your older brother, He Yao.

81
00:13:04,375 --> 00:13:05,541
You've met before.

82
00:13:05,666 --> 00:13:06,750
Do you remember?

83
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:10,208
He'll be living with us from now on.

84
00:13:15,625 --> 00:13:16,958
Yeah, I know.

85
00:13:18,666 --> 00:13:19,708
I'm going to my room.

86
00:13:20,083 --> 00:13:21,083
Your bed...

87
00:13:24,750 --> 00:13:26,791
Changhuan is a bit shy around strangers.

88
00:15:39,708 --> 00:15:40,708
Mom.

89
00:15:42,142 --> 00:15:42,976
Changhuan, you're back.

90
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Here, give it to me.

91
00:15:44,958 --> 00:15:45,791
What do you want to eat?

92
00:15:45,875 --> 00:15:46,875
Mom will make it for you.

93
00:15:47,375 --> 00:15:48,583
Today I want to eat...

94
00:15:49,750 --> 00:15:50,750
Yao,

95
00:15:51,375 --> 00:15:52,625
what happened to you?

96
00:15:53,166 --> 00:15:54,458
How did you cut your head?

97
00:15:55,541 --> 00:15:56,416
Come sit down.

98
00:15:56,417 --> 00:15:57,537
Let me disinfect it for you.

99
00:15:57,833 --> 00:15:58,833
It's fine, Auntie.

100
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,125
I accidentally fell.

101
00:16:00,291 --> 00:16:01,791
Your head is bleeding.

102
00:16:03,958 --> 00:16:05,457
How did this happen?

103
00:16:05,458 --> 00:16:06,750
How could you be so careless?

104
00:16:07,166 --> 00:16:08,166
It's fine, Auntie.

105
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,080
Let me clean it a bit more.

106
00:16:12,291 --> 00:16:13,541
I'll be gentle.

107
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,125
You're too careless. Let's change it.

108
00:16:24,708 --> 00:16:26,290
Come on, Dad is working overtime.

109
00:16:26,291 --> 00:16:27,291
Let's eat first.

110
00:16:36,208 --> 00:16:37,708
Come on, eat up.

111
00:16:39,083 --> 00:16:40,083
Here.

112
00:16:43,375 --> 00:16:44,000
Today,

113
00:16:44,001 --> 00:16:45,666
Mr. Wang called specifically to say

114
00:16:45,958 --> 00:16:47,458
that for this midterm exam,

115
00:16:47,625 --> 00:16:50,250
the top two students in the
grade are both in our family.

116
00:16:51,875 --> 00:16:53,291
I'm so happy.

117
00:16:53,958 --> 00:16:56,000
Auntie, Changhuan is the amazing one.

118
00:16:57,041 --> 00:16:58,625
For that big math problem this time,

119
00:16:58,708 --> 00:17:00,108
his solution was incredibly unique.

120
00:17:00,166 --> 00:17:01,606
Even the teacher didn't think of it.

121
00:17:03,250 --> 00:17:04,250
Really?

122
00:17:04,666 --> 00:17:05,958
You are both my pride and joy.

123
00:17:06,708 --> 00:17:07,708
Auntie,

124
00:17:08,208 --> 00:17:10,708
Changhuan and I will definitely
keep up the good work.

125
00:17:13,708 --> 00:17:14,916
I'm full.

126
00:17:18,875 --> 00:17:19,875
This time,

127
00:17:20,666 --> 00:17:21,666
I didn't do well.

128
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:24,958
Changhuan! Changhuan!

129
00:17:27,958 --> 00:17:29,333
What's with that kid...

130
00:18:30,083 --> 00:18:32,333
Do you want some water?

131
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,280
Drinking too much water at night

132
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:38,541
is bad for your kidneys.

133
00:19:00,250 --> 00:19:01,625
Still studying this late?

134
00:19:02,083 --> 00:19:03,958
It's for the Math Olympiad, right?

135
00:19:05,083 --> 00:19:06,416
For this problem, it...

136
00:19:06,791 --> 00:19:07,791
I'll study on my own.

137
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,208
Ever since we were kids,

138
00:21:09,958 --> 00:21:11,458
I've tried my hardest,

139
00:21:13,625 --> 00:21:15,416
but it seems I'm always
one step behind you.

140
00:21:20,458 --> 00:21:21,458
He Yao,

141
00:21:22,416 --> 00:21:23,583
in your eyes,

142
00:21:24,625 --> 00:21:26,666
do I always need you to take care of me?

143
00:21:28,666 --> 00:21:30,041
You're my younger brother.

144
00:21:30,791 --> 00:21:32,207
Of course I have to take care of you.

145
00:21:32,208 --> 00:21:33,333
I'm not your brother.

146
00:21:34,375 --> 00:21:35,750
I'm Shen Changhuan.

147
00:21:38,708 --> 00:21:40,041
I don't care what you think.

148
00:21:41,041 --> 00:21:42,875
You...

149
00:21:49,416 --> 00:21:51,166
Since we're tied together now,

150
00:21:51,875 --> 00:21:53,125
this path,

151
00:21:54,208 --> 00:21:56,000
we have to walk it together.

152
00:21:56,416 --> 00:21:58,041
You don't have the option to ditch me.

153
00:21:59,916 --> 00:22:01,041
You never did.

154
00:22:23,666 --> 00:22:25,916
The infection in your
wound is getting worse.

155
00:22:26,458 --> 00:22:27,818
We need to find antibiotics, fast.

156
00:22:31,250 --> 00:22:32,291
Let's rest for a bit.

157
00:22:41,750 --> 00:22:43,125
Wait here and don't move.

158
00:22:43,291 --> 00:22:44,891
I'll check if there's water in the well.

159
00:22:45,500 --> 00:22:46,500
Come back!

160
00:23:00,625 --> 00:23:01,625
Why did you come over?

161
00:23:03,083 --> 00:23:04,323
I wanted to keep an eye on you.

162
00:23:05,791 --> 00:23:07,083
I told you not to move.

163
00:23:16,708 --> 00:23:17,708
Don't move.

164
00:23:32,541 --> 00:23:33,541
Hey, friends.

165
00:23:35,958 --> 00:23:37,208
Where are you folks from?
